    <briefdescription>
<para>Manages a sequence of passes over a particular unit of IR. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A pass manager contains a sequence of passes to run over a particular unit of IR (e.g. Functions, Modules). It is itself a valid pass over that unit of IR, and when run over some given IR will run each of its contained passes in sequence. <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_pass" kindref="compound">Pass</ref> managers are the primary and most basic building block of a pass pipeline.</para>
<para>When you run a pass manager, you provide an <computeroutput><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_analysis_manager" kindref="compound">AnalysisManager&lt;IRUnitT&gt;</ref></computeroutput> argument. The pass manager will propagate that analysis manager to each pass it runs, and will call the analysis manager&apos;s invalidation routine with the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_preserved_analyses" kindref="compound">PreservedAnalyses</ref> of each pass it runs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
